---@field StartDate? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowStringDateTime The date and time, in ISO-8601 Extended format, for when you want the maintenance window to become active. StartDate allows you to delay activation of the maintenance window until the specified future date.
---@field EndDate? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowStringDateTime The date and time, in ISO-8601 Extended format, for when you want the maintenance window to become inactive. EndDate allows you to set a date and time in the future when the maintenance window will no longer run.
---@field Schedule? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowSchedule The schedule of the maintenance window in the form of a cron or rate expression.
---@field ScheduleTimezone? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowTimezone The time zone that the scheduled maintenance window executions are based on, in Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) format. For example: "America/Los_Angeles", "UTC", or "Asia/Seoul". For more information, see the Time Zone Database on the IANA website.
---@field ScheduleOffset? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowOffset The number of days to wait after the date and time specified by a cron expression before running the maintenance window.
---@field Duration? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowDurationHours The duration of the maintenance window in hours.
---@field Cutoff? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowCutoff The number of hours before the end of the maintenance window that Amazon Web Services Systems Manager stops scheduling new tasks for execution.
---@field AllowUnassociatedTargets? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowAllowUnassociatedTargets Whether targets must be registered with the maintenance window before tasks can be defined for those targets.
---@field Enabled? aws.ssm.MaintenanceWindowEnabled Whether the maintenance window is enabled.
---@field Replace? aws.ssm.Boolean If True, then all fields that are required by the CreateMaintenanceWindow operation are also required for this API request. Optional fields that aren't specified are set to null.

